                "text": "This report reviews customer complaints received between January and March. Complaints rose by 18% compared with the previous quarter, mainly due to late deliveries in the North region (62% of all complaints). Our analysis shows that the main cause is the shortage of drivers at the Leeds depot. We recommend hiring four temporary drivers for six months (estimated cost: £48,000) and reviewing delivery routes. We expect this to reduce complaints by at least 30% by September. We ask the operations committee to approve the budget by 30 April.",
